Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: plasma-nm-vpn
Source: https://github.com/alldevic/plasma-nm-vpn
Comment: The core packages also ship third-party core binaries, which are not
 part of this source package:
  - plasma-nm-vpn-sb: /usr/lib/plasma-nm-vpn/bin/sing-box, sing-box 1.14.4 from
    https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box, unchanged release binary;
    license GPL-3+ with the additional term below (License: GPL-3+-sing-box).
  - plasma-nm-vpn-xray: /usr/lib/plasma-nm-vpn/bin/xray, Xray-core 26.11.9 from
    https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core, unchanged release binary; license MPL-2.0.
  - plasma-nm-vpn-amneziawg: /usr/lib/plasma-nm-vpn/bin/amneziawg-go, built from
    https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amneziawg-go tag v3.1.20261116; license
    Expat. /usr/lib/plasma-nm-vpn/bin/awg, built from
    https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amneziawg-tools tag v3.1.20260812; license
    GPL-2.
 The sources of the GPL cores, with their Go dependencies, are published next
 to the packages in each release. The cores' own license files are installed in
 /usr/share/doc/<package>/.

